  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🌞 Altmer Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Long, graceful high elf names from the Summerset Isles, in the style of Ancano and Elenwen."
    },
    "intro": "The Altmer, or <a href=\"high-elf-name-generator.html\">high elves</a>, of the Summerset Isles think very highly of themselves, and their names sound like it: long, flowing and formal. In Skyrim you meet them as Ancano at the College of Winterhold and as the Thalmor's Elenwen and Ondolemar. This **Altmer name generator** gives you names in the same style, for Skyrim, Elder Scrolls Online or your own Tamriel story.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What Altmer names sound like",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Long:</strong> three or four syllables is normal. Ondolemar, Ancarion.</li><li><strong>Soft consonants</strong> (l, n, r, m) and open vowels, with few harsh sounds.</li><li><strong>Male names</strong> often end in <em>-o</em>, <em>-ar</em> or <em>-il</em>: Ancano, Estormo and Ondolemar in Skyrim.</li><li><strong>Female names</strong> often end in <em>-we</em>, <em>-wen</em> or <em>-a</em>: Elenwen, Nirya and Faralda.</li></ul><p>Altmer names are usually used alone. That suits a people who believe they're descended from the gods and don't feel the need to explain their family.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Altmer in Skyrim",
        "content": "<p>Most Altmer in Skyrim belong to the Thalmor, the government of the Aldmeri Dominion. <strong>Elenwen</strong> is the Thalmor ambassador, <strong>Ondolemar</strong> commands the Thalmor in Markarth, and <strong>Ancano</strong> is the Thalmor adviser who causes trouble at the College of Winterhold.</p><p>Not every Altmer is Thalmor. <strong>Faralda</strong> and <strong>Nirya</strong> teach at the College, and <strong>Ancarion</strong> lives in Solitude. An Altmer character who isn't Thalmor has an easy source of tension in any Nord town.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Using the names",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Let it be long.</strong> An Altmer won't shorten their name for anyone, which says a lot about them.</li><li><strong>Add a title if they're important:</strong> Justiciar, First Emissary, Magister.</li><li><strong>Elder Scrolls Online</strong> needs unique names, and a long Altmer name is more likely to be free.</li></ul><p>For other races of Tamriel, see the <a href=\"dunmer-name-generator.html\">Dunmer</a>, <a href=\"khajiit-name-generator.html\">Khajiit</a> and <a href=\"nord-name-generator.html\">Nord</a> name generators.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Do Altmer have last names?",
        "answer": "Usually not in Skyrim: Ancano, Elenwen and Ondolemar all go by one name. Titles, like Justiciar, are more common than surnames."
      },
      {
        "question": "Who are the Thalmor?",
        "answer": "The ruling government of the Aldmeri Dominion, led by the Altmer. In Skyrim they enforce the ban on worshipping Talos."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are these names from the games?",
        "answer": "No. They're new names in the same style, so your character won't share a name with someone in Tamriel."
      }
    ]
  }
